**F6 — semantics change: watchdog timeout now permanently poisons the iterator (`abandoned = true`) even if the adapter wanted to retry moveNext.** Previously after a TimeoutException the old code also cancelled `_inner` — moveNext after that threw StateError. Equivalent. Not a regression.

**F7 — the swallow condition `(cancelToken?.isCancelled ?? false)`:** token cancelled but stream NOT abandoned and body open — swallows ALL errors including non-transport ones. This is the preserved documented behavior ("The injected 'connection closed' error is therefore swallowed here whenever [cancelToken] is cancelled"). Pre-existing intent, fine.

**F8 — `onPause`/`onResume` + abandoned:** after abandonment the transformer chain is being cancelled; pause requests from the chain on `body`... fine.

**F9 — Memory/perf:** one extra StreamController + subscription per SSE response. Negligible.

**F10 — Zone capture subtlety:** `rawSub = response.stream.listen(...)` — the handlers run in the zone active at `createSseIterator` call time. The error swallowing decision reads `abandoned`/`cancelToken` — no zone dependency. If the CREATING zone errors... the handler itself doesn't throw (guarded). ✓

**F11 — `runGuarded` helper in tests: `(_, _) => escaped = true`** — wildcards OK on sdk 3.12.

**F12 — test flakiness:** 20ms settle delay — pragmatic; errors from rawSub's onError are swallowed synchronously in the handler (no zone escape at all), so the delay is just belt-and-braces. The `expectLater(iterator.moveNext(), throwsA(...))` with 60ms watchdog — deterministic enough.

**F13 — `_connectionClosed` in test references a real URL (api.z.ai)** — just a Uri object, never dialed. Fine.

**F14 — Duplicated swallow logic:** the `onError` condition `abandoned || token.isCancelled || body.isClosed` and `onData`'s `!abandoned` — slight asymmetry (F2). Also `body.isClosed` check in onError protects against addError-after-close. OK.

**F15 — Missing coverage: the `onDone` unstick claim isn't directly tested** (no test asserting the lazy cancellation completes after abandonment without onDone). Minor.

**F16 — Docs:** the updated doc comment on `createSseIterator` is thorough. AGENTS.md §model_roles mentions watchdogs; no AGENTS.md update needed (internal detail).

**F17 — `AbortedError` behavior in anthropic after cancel:** `if (cancelToken?.isCancelled ?? false) throw const AbortedError();` — after a token abort, moveNext loop ends (errors swallowed / data dropped) → done → loop exits → sees token cancelled → AbortedError. Unchanged by this PR. ✓

**F18 — one more race: token cancel fires WHILE a live error is propagating.** rawSub onError → checks `cancelToken?.isCancelled` — if the token was JUST cancelled (flag set synchronously in `CancelTokenSource.cancel`; listeners scheduled via microtask), the flag is already true → swallow. Previously: old handleError also checked `cancelToken.isCancelled` at error-forward time. Same. ✓

